ID: PD-2026-008 (no public advisory, Portadesign hardening)
Package: pimcore/pimcore
Verified: 11.5.4, 11.5.14.1
Summary: Mail::send() and getBodyHtmlRendered() rendered mail content as a Twig template more than once: an email document is rendered with the mail parameters and the result is rendered again, and the plain text part was derived from the already rendered HTML through a third pass. A parameter holding template syntax (newsletter subscriber first name in confirmation and newsletter mails, directly or through a getter of an object parameter, escaped or not) was executed. After the document render every {{ }}, {% %} and {# #} start that is not part of a snippet found in the document's own editables is encoded as &#123;, so only placeholders written by editors reach the second pass, which still receives the real parameters. Placeholders inside other documents embedded by the template (snippets, renderlets) are no longer evaluated. The plain text part is converted from the rendered HTML without another pass.

